# Tutorial: Sessions

This tutorial describes how sessions work. To read it again later, use the
`clawp_read_tutorial` tool with topic `system_sessions`.

## Sessions

A session within the framework represents your context window. It is a list of
messages with metadata. Sessions are append-only. When a session needs to be
changed (e.g. to compact your context), it is archived and a new one created.
The system will inform you at the start of a session that a new one has started
and for what reason.

Sessions are append-only and messages within a session are immutable. Each
message is uniquely identified within a session by its `seq_in_session`, the
sequence number of the message (starting at 0).
